{
    "cells":  [
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "# NMDAR / GluN2B inhibitor activity prediction\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "This notebook presents the reproducible machine-learning workflow for the NMDAR (GluN2B) inhibitor project. It loads the prepared descriptor and fingerprint datasets, checks the train/validation/test partitions, trains representative classifiers, evaluates predictions on the held-out test set, and provides a reusable prediction helper.\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "**Scope:** molecular feature generation is represented by the prepared project datasets in this repository.\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "The binary target is `Activity`, where the project data encodes active and inactive compounds as numeric classes."
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "## Project files and data split\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "The notebook expects these files to be in the same directory as the notebook:\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "- `final_ml_dataset_train.csv` model fitting data\n",
                                     "- `final_ml_dataset_validation.csv` model validation data\n",
                                     "- `final_ml_dataset_test.csv` final held-out evaluation data\n",
                                     "- `Model_Performance_Comparison.csv` onsolidated project benchmark results\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "The prepared feature table contains 249 scaled descriptor columns and RDKit, Morgan, and MACCS fingerprint columns."
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "code",
                      "execution_count":  null,
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "outputs":  [

                                  ],
                      "source":  [
                                     "from pathlib import Path\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "import numpy as np\n",
                                     "import pandas as pd\n",
                                     "from IPython.display import display\n",
                                     "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
                                     "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
                                     "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
                                     "    accuracy_score,\n",
                                     "    classification_report,\n",
                                     "    confusion_matrix,\n",
                                     "    f1_score,\n",
                                     "    precision_score,\n",
                                     "    recall_score,\n",
                                     "    roc_auc_score,\n",
                                     ")\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "PROJECT_DIR = Path.cwd()\n",
                                     "TARGET = \"Activity\"\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "def require_file(filename: str) -\u003e Path:\n",
                                     "    path = PROJECT_DIR / filename\n",
                                     "    if not path.exists():\n",
                                     "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
                                     "            f\"Required project file was not found: {path}. \"\n",
                                     "            \"Run this notebook from the repository directory.\"\n",
                                     "        )\n",
                                     "    return path\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "train = pd.read_csv(require_file(\"final_ml_dataset_train.csv\"))\n",
                                     "validation = pd.read_csv(require_file(\"final_ml_dataset_validation.csv\"))\n",
                                     "test = pd.read_csv(require_file(\"final_ml_dataset_test.csv\"))\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "for name, frame in ((\"train\", train), (\"validation\", validation), (\"test\", test)):\n",
                                     "    if TARGET not in frame.columns:\n",
                                     "        raise ValueError(f\"{TARGET!r} is missing from the {name} dataset\")\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "X_train, y_train = train.drop(columns=TARGET), train[TARGET].astype(int)\n",
                                     "X_validation, y_validation = validation.drop(columns=TARGET), validation[TARGET].astype(int)\n",
                                     "X_test, y_test = test.drop(columns=TARGET), test[TARGET].astype(int)\n",
                                     "if list(X_train.columns) != list(X_validation.columns) or list(X_train.columns) != list(X_test.columns):\n",
                                     "    raise ValueError(\"Train, validation, and test feature columns must match in the same order\")\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "print(f\"Train: {train.shape}; validation: {validation.shape}; test: {test.shape}\")\n",
                                     "print(f\"Feature count: {X_train.shape[1]}\")\n",
                                     "display(pd.DataFrame({\"split\": [\"train\", \"validation\", \"test\"], \"active\": [int((y_train == 1).sum()), int((y_validation == 1).sum()), int((y_test == 1).sum())], \"inactive\": [int((y_train == 0).sum()), int((y_validation == 0).sum()), int((y_test == 0).sum())]}))"
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "code",
                      "execution_count":  null,
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "outputs":  [

                                  ],
                      "source":  [
                                     "feature_groups = {\n",
                                     "    \"scaled_descriptors\": [c for c in X_train.columns if c.startswith(\"Scaled_\")],\n",
                                     "    \"rdkit_fingerprints\": [c for c in X_train.columns if c.startswith(\"RDKit_\")],\n",
                                     "    \"morgan_fingerprints\": [c for c in X_train.columns if c.startswith(\"Morgan_\")],\n",
                                     "    \"maccs_fingerprints\": [c for c in X_train.columns if c.startswith(\"MACCS_\")],\n",
                                     "}\n",
                                     "display(pd.DataFrame({\"feature_group\": list(feature_groups), \"features\": [len(v) for v in feature_groups.values()]}))"
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "## Representative models\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "The descriptor model uses logistic regression because the descriptor columns are already scaled. The fingerprint model uses a random forest, which is suitable for sparse binary fingerprints and produces class probabilities for downstream ranking. Validation data is used for a sanity check; the test set remains the final held-out evaluation."
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "code",
                      "execution_count":  null,
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "outputs":  [

                                  ],
                      "source":  [
                                     "def evaluate(model, X, y, label):\n",
                                     "    predictions = model.predict(X)\n",
                                     "    probabilities = model.predict_proba(X)[:, 1] if hasattr(model, \"predict_proba\") else None\n",
                                     "    result = {\n",
                                     "        \"model\": label,\n",
                                     "        \"accuracy\": accuracy_score(y, predictions),\n",
                                     "        \"precision\": precision_score(y, predictions, zero_division=0),\n",
                                     "        \"recall\": recall_score(y, predictions, zero_division=0),\n",
                                     "        \"f1\": f1_score(y, predictions, zero_division=0),\n",
                                     "        \"roc_auc\": roc_auc_score(y, probabilities) if probabilities is not None else np.nan,\n",
                                     "    }\n",
                                     "    print(label)\n",
                                     "    print(classification_report(y, predictions, target_names=[\"Inactive\", \"Active\"], zero_division=0))\n",
                                     "    display(pd.DataFrame([result]))\n",
                                     "    display(pd.DataFrame(confusion_matrix(y, predictions), index=[\"Actual inactive\", \"Actual active\"], columns=[\"Predicted inactive\", \"Predicted active\"]))\n",
                                     "    return result\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "descriptor_columns = feature_groups[\"scaled_descriptors\"]\n",
                                     "morgan_columns = feature_groups[\"morgan_fingerprints\"]\n",
                                     "descriptor_model = LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42)\n",
                                     "descriptor_model.fit(X_train[descriptor_columns], y_train)\n",
                                     "evaluate(descriptor_model, X_validation[descriptor_columns], y_validation, \"Logistic regression / scaled descriptors\")\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "morgan_model = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
                                     "    n_estimators=500, max_depth=25, min_samples_split=5,\n",
                                     "    class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42, n_jobs=-1,\n",
                                     ")\n",
                                     "morgan_model.fit(X_train[morgan_columns], y_train)\n",
                                     "evaluate(morgan_model, X_validation[morgan_columns], y_validation, \"Random forest / Morgan fingerprints\")"
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "## Final held-out test evaluation\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "These metrics are calculated only after model fitting and validation checks. They should be reported together with the project benchmark table rather than treated as a replacement for independent experimental validation."
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "code",
                      "execution_count":  null,
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "outputs":  [

                                  ],
                      "source":  [
                                     "test_results = pd.DataFrame([\n",
                                     "    evaluate(descriptor_model, X_test[descriptor_columns], y_test, \"Test: logistic regression / scaled descriptors\"),\n",
                                     "    evaluate(morgan_model, X_test[morgan_columns], y_test, \"Test: random forest / Morgan fingerprints\"),\n",
                                     "])\n",
                                     "test_results"
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "## Existing project benchmark\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "The repository also contains the consolidated benchmark generated during model comparison. Loading it here preserves the projectÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s documented results without rerunning every hyperparameter search."
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "code",
                      "execution_count":  null,
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "outputs":  [

                                  ],
                      "source":  [
                                     "benchmark = pd.read_csv(require_file(\"Model_Performance_Comparison.csv\"))\n",
                                     "benchmark.sort_values(\"ROC-AUC\", ascending=False).head(10)"
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "## Prediction helper\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "Pass one row containing the same prepared feature columns as the training data. The helper returns the predicted class and active-class probability from both representative models."
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "code",
                      "execution_count":  null,
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "outputs":  [

                                  ],
                      "source":  [
                                     "def predict_activity(feature_row: pd.DataFrame) -\u003e pd.DataFrame:\n",
                                     "    missing = [c for c in X_train.columns if c not in feature_row.columns]\n",
                                     "    if missing:\n",
                                     "        raise ValueError(f\"Prediction input is missing {len(missing)} prepared feature columns\")\n",
                                     "    row = feature_row.loc[:, X_train.columns]\n",
                                     "    return pd.DataFrame({\n",
                                     "        \"descriptor_prediction\": descriptor_model.predict(row[descriptor_columns]),\n",
                                     "        \"descriptor_active_probability\": descriptor_model.predict_proba(row[descriptor_columns])[:, 1],\n",
                                     "        \"morgan_prediction\": morgan_model.predict(row[morgan_columns]),\n",
                                     "        \"morgan_active_probability\": morgan_model.predict_proba(row[morgan_columns])[:, 1],\n",
                                     "    })\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "predict_activity(X_test.iloc[[0]])"
                                 ]
                  },
                  {
                      "cell_type":  "markdown",
                      "metadata":  {

                                   },
                      "source":  [
                                     "## Reproducibility notes\n",
                                     "\n",
                                     "- Run the notebook from the repository directory so the relative data paths resolve correctly.\n",
                                     "- Keep the train/validation/test partitions fixed when comparing models.\n",
                                     "- The prediction helper expects already prepared descriptors/fingerprints; it does not calculate features from a SMILES string.\n",
                                 ]
                  }
              ],
